{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat assignments/T-P-resource-observe.md'","aggregated_output":"# Assignment T-P (campaign c2-resume, host x86-main, owner: Claude Opus; worker: Codex)\nQuestion: a small portable resource-observation capability with explicit backends; x86 implements the discrete-NVIDIA + Linux backends and drafts the common contract that the Jetson lead will extend with a tegrastats backend.\nRead: bin/lab (gpu_state, cid_cgroup, read_int and the memory sampler in cmd_run) to see current ad-hoc sampling.\nAllowed writes: cc/resource_observe/** and artifacts/codexP/. Do not modify bin/lab.\nDeliver: cc/resource_observe/observe.py (stdlib-only Python 3.12): `sample()` -> dict with schema `resource-sample/0`: ts (UTC ISO + monotonic), host_id, backend list, and fields each as {value, unit, source, scope, status: ok|unavailable|error, reason}. Fields: gpu.memory.used/total (nvidia-smi query; scope=device-total, includes other processes), gpu.util, gpu.temp, gpu.power, gpu.clocks, gpu.compute_apps (pid, used MiB), host.mem total/available/swap (/proc/meminfo), cgroup memory.current/peak/swap/io rbytes for a given cgroup path, process rss for given pid. Missing tool/field -> status unavailable + reason, never 0. `sample_series(interval, duration|until)` with loss accounting (expected vs obtained samples, max gap). CLI: `observe.py once|watch --interval --out jsonl`. CONTRACT.md: common fields, units, scope/attribution rules (e.g. device-total vs per-process; cgroups do not account driver/GPU allocations; on Jetson shared DRAM must not be double-counted as gpu+host), extension mechanism for platform fields, and what Jetson should implement (tegrastats fields). Fixtures: captured real `nvidia-smi --query-gpu=... --format=csv` and /proc/meminfo outputs from THIS host (you may run nvidia-smi read-only queries; no other GPU use), plus malformed/missing variants (e.g. \"[N/A]\", \"[Not Supported]\", empty output, nvidia-smi absent). pytest tests over fixtures.\nLimits: 35 min, no network, no Docker, no GPU workloads, no clock/power changes. Final message: files, pytest result, contract summary, gaps.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
